{"title":"2008 Mock ARML 1 Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(30_Seconds)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (30 Seconds)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_1_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Regular_polygon\" title=\"Regular polygon\">regular</a> hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/8029902caf855d940e465d04ff40101d8850c3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDEF$\" width=\"86\" height=\"13\" /> with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65e4f2d5cc59e5ffbed3734130e8c45b643adc91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a771251838750a4cb9926c5e2b03324b2b2edae7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.  Compute the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a7a248cfd02095e2a009f811d5732a9bea9d595.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_1_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2adda0608ac45c1f95b0abb8a8656cf1274ebc3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pointpen = black; pathpen = black + linewidth(0.62); pair v(int n){ return dir(n * 60); }  D(MP(&quot;A&quot;,v(0))--MP(&quot;B&quot;,v(1),N)--MP(&quot;C&quot;,v(2),N)--MP(&quot;D&quot;,v(3),SW)--MP(&quot;E&quot;,v(4))--MP(&quot;F&quot;,v(5))--cycle); D(v(0)--v(3));D(v(1)--v(5));D(v(1)--v(3));D(v(2)--v(4)); D(D(MP(&quot;G&quot;,IP(v(0)--v(3),v(1)--v(5)),NE))--D(MP(&quot;H&quot;,IP(v(1)--v(3),v(2)--v(4)),NW)),dashed); D(MP(&quot;H&#39;&quot;,IP(v(2)--v(4),v(0)--v(3)),SW)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"232\" /></center>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f783df024abc16be6be7f4d262c926e8f24fc6a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H&#39;$\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular\" title=\"Perpendicular\">perpendicular</a> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/2/f52ad9ae2045af1a306a7815747c10c997abc4f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CDA$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> is an inscribed angle with measure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/7/287877af5b4b369c96e03facac65666037ec7b5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{120}{2} = 60^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/4/b9462861a2d7d2b719e690278a901deafea9864d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CDH&#39;$\" width=\"66\" height=\"14\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/0/8f040866096861a91f1b9c755be19cf0849ae480.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90 \\triangle$\" width=\"114\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/4142c4967fac2fee7afb3d235f347bcdf5fa5642.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DH&#39; = \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"72\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efb34fc778017bb63ca5b603a9ac32b112c06f8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH&#39; = BG = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"139\" height=\"41\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/9/a093fc94300d9743cd16ba2a71cbb3e6eab6f828.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H&#39;G = CB = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"124\" height=\"16\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/7/1371dbfe7d02112137911b105843cdc53d4983c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DH&#39;H \\sim \\triangle DGB$\" width=\"154\" height=\"14\" /> by ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/7/217aedbdc339bacc8ba075a2ec16902b098194e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/4/af4b49f99ae27a99bab13e92176530d457fcc3b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HH&#39; = BG/3 = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"164\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cac1b04ba52bf3bf862790d1855f62a0afe91882.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HG^2 = H&#39;H^2 + H&#39;H^2 = \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}\\right)^2 + 1 = \\frac{13}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"339\" height=\"56\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/967dcea484463f43ada309f5431e33a7fe408e57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HG = \\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{39}}{6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"104\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_1_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We use coordinates. Consider the diagram in Solution 1. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66c8bd013ea7bc3e200bdbb0adbdb7706c592787.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />. By 30-60-90\ntriangle ratios, we can get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/4/a046ff30f8cf3c13c31b1c46b8969351e2080934.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=(\\frac12, \\frac{\\sqrt3}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"104\" height=\"43\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b76f9f1ee2f863dfebc82a9821c5076f19c1b974.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H&#39;=(\\frac12, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"88\" height=\"37\" />. In addition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/0/c3095fd46ba1bbae4a911eba068b46ef038ac70d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=(\\frac32, \\frac{\\sqrt3}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"101\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/6/9569821d81f3ff1f008c607b014cd305b5235fcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E=(\\frac12, -\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"115\" height=\"41\" />. The line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/e/95eaca439ccbf2863a43b05f4de566ccdabdc392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CE}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> is represented by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da5cdb297400b28196aeb8ea617b007db7dc9c23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" />. The line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> is represented by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/36920a37675bda7ef5a6de6a0139c946dd1469cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{3}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"72\" height=\"41\" />. The intersection (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />) is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/3359efe1dd5e9bc969f58c0e1742ae8e6f623838.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac12, \\frac{\\sqrt3}{6})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"62\" height=\"41\" />. We additionaly can get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65a9d6cadf5e3a60dd729213618714e5e3f2acb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G=(\\frac32,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"81\" height=\"37\" />. Then, by\nthe distance formula, the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a7a248cfd02095e2a009f811d5732a9bea9d595.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/d/26dd1fad51d5d792c5d2c7d49193eb92d9e33b34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{1^2+\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{6}\\right)^2}=\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{39}}{6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -24px\" width=\"194\" height=\"64\" />.\n</p><p>~yofro\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.2830_Seconds.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(30_Seconds)\">Solution 3 (30 Seconds)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_1_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (30 Seconds)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Use the diagram in Solution 1.\nNotice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/7/3f7300c811c15f2668975f41f9fe7da79b3b31ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DHH&#39;\\sim \\triangle BHC$\" width=\"155\" height=\"14\" />. The ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e1a1a7adf986532b7598e896785a56c785f779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3ad957daab97896400b8b9e87f389a4225af0b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DH&#39;=\\frac12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"72\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/8/388ae1c6e305c803fcd7fa55573c7aaf574dab9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. Letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/7/237256eaceb67913f12d0907629be9b30a5c9a0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HH&#39;=x$\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4ff9de630bc3968df2c92426a2468f49d56f73cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3x=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\implies x=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"182\" height=\"41\" />. Then by the Pythagorean Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99d5a98a1ead89fb215f0d00532c2496ae81d243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GH=\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{39}}{6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"104\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>~yofro\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_1_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_1\" title=\"2008 Mock ARML 1\">2008 Mock ARML 1</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_1_Problems\" title=\"2008 Mock ARML 1 Problems\">Problems</a></b>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=206547\">Source</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_1_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 Mock ARML 1 Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_1_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 Mock ARML 1 Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" align=\"center\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_1_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 Mock ARML 1 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_1_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 Mock ARML 1 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_1_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 Mock ARML 1 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_1_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 Mock ARML 1 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_1_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 Mock ARML 1 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_1_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 Mock ARML 1 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_Mock_ARML_1_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 Mock ARML 1 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017215630\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 295/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 987/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 70/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8820/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.718      1 Template:Mock_ARML_box\n100.00%    7.718      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6941:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017215630 and revision id 139093. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}